{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The preparations of the heart in man, and the answer of the tongue, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the ways of a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " clean in his own eyes; but the LORD weigheth the spirits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Commit thy works to the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD hath made all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for himself: yes, even the wicked for the day of evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " proud in heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an abomination to the LORD: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "join",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in hand, he shall not be unpunished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By mercy and truth iniquity is purged: and by the fear of the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " depart from evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When a man's ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a little with righteousness, than great revenues without right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man's heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A divine sentence ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the lips of the king: his mouth transgresseth not in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A just weight and balance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD'S: all the weights of the bag ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an abomination to kings to commit wickedness: for the throne is established by righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Righteous lips ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the delight of kings; and they love him that speaketh right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wrath of a king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " messengers of death: but a wise man will pacify it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the light of a king's countenance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " life; and his favor ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a cloud of the latter rain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to get wisdom than gold? and to get understanding rather to be chosen than silver?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The highway of the upright ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to depart from evil: he that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pride ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "goeth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before destruction, and a haughty spirit before a fall.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of a humble spirit with the lowly, than to divide the spoil with the proud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that handleth a matter wisely shall find good: and whoever trusteth in the LORD, happy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Understanding ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a well-spring of life to him that hath it: but the instruction of fools ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " folly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heart of the wise teacheth his mouth, and addeth learning to his lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pleasant words ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a honey-comb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is a way that seemeth right to a man, but the end of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the ways of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that laboreth laboreth for himself; for his mouth craveth it of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An ungodly man diggeth up evil: and in his lips ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a burning fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A froward man soweth strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A violent man enticeth his neighbor, and leadeth him into the way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shutteth his eyes to devise froward things: moving his lips he bringeth evil to pass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The hoary head ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a crown of glory, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it is found in the way of righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " slow to anger ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit, than he that taketh a city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.16.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lot is cast into the lap: but the whole disposing of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
